{
  "id": "COMPOUND:31122 - PROTEIN:6323",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence strongly suggests a mechanistic link between 3-O-Beta-D-Glucopyranosyl-(1->4)-Alpha-L-Rhamnopyranosylcannogenin and DNA polymerase iota, through a series of target interactions involving the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex. This compound is identified as a target of multiple molecules, including Sid124895033 and a structurally related compound, which in turn target DNA polymerase iota. The presence of multiple pathways converging on DNA polymerase iota through the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex indicates a potential role for this compound in modulating DNA polymerase activity. The evidence supports a mechanism where the compound may interact with the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex, potentially influencing its function and thereby affecting DNA polymerase iota. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible regulatory role for the compound in the DNA replication process, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be elucidated.",
